Author: Liu Zheng <liuzheng@uniontech.com>
Date:   Mon Sep 15 10:00:00 2026
Subject: Fix QSvgFontEngine::glyphIndex signature to match QFontEngine 6.8

The base class QFontEngine::glyphIndex in QtGui 6.8 private header has
the signature:
    virtual glyph_t glyphIndex(uint ucs4, uint variationSelector = 0) const = 0;
The QSvgFontEngine override used the old single-argument signature, so
the `override` did not actually override the pure virtual function.
As a result QSvgFontEngine remained abstract and could not be
instantiated, causing build failures:
  - error: 'glyphIndex' marked 'override', but does not override
  - error: invalid new-expression of abstract class type 'QSvgFontEngine'

Align the override with the base class signature so the class is
concrete and compiles against QtGui 6.8.

---

Index: qt6-declarative/src/quickvectorimage/generator/qsvgvisitorimpl.cpp
===================================================================
--- qt6-declarative.orig/src/quickvectorimage/generator/qsvgvisitorimpl.cpp
+++ qt6-declarative/src/quickvectorimage/generator/qsvgvisitorimpl.cpp
@@ -452,7 +452,7 @@ namespace {

         QFontEngine *cloneWithSize(qreal size) const override;

-        glyph_t glyphIndex(uint ucs4) const override;
+        glyph_t glyphIndex(uint ucs4, uint variationSelector = 0) const override;
         int stringToCMap(const QChar *str,
                          int len,
                          QGlyphLayout *glyphs,
@@ -495,8 +495,9 @@ namespace {
         return QFixed::fromReal(m_font->m_unitsPerEm);
     }

-    glyph_t QSvgFontEngine::glyphIndex(uint ucs4) const
+    glyph_t QSvgFontEngine::glyphIndex(uint ucs4, uint variationSelector) const
     {
+        Q_UNUSED(variationSelector);
         if (ucs4 < USHRT_MAX && m_font->m_glyphs.contains(QChar(ushort(ucs4))))
             return glyph_t(ucs4);

